- [N1] Omitted trace (input 1): i1:To start the process for ACME, -> i2:begin with the New Resupply Cycle -> i3:then Check Levels of Inventory. -> i4:If the inventory is below or equal to the minimum, generate an Equal to or below minimum Report. -> i6:If the report indicates that the inventory is equal to or below the minimum, create Purchase Orders (POs). -> i10:If the PO is created, it needs to be reviewed. -> i8:If the PO is rejected, it needs to be reworked. -> i11:If the PO needs to be reworked, it needs to be created again. -> i6:If the report indicates that the inventory is equal to or below the minimum, create Purchase Orders (POs).
- [N2] Omitted trace (input 3): i1:To start the process for ACME, -> i2:begin with the New Resupply Cycle -> i3:then Check Levels of Inventory. -> i4:If the inventory is below or equal to the minimum, generate an Equal to or below minimum Report. -> i6:If the report indicates that the inventory is equal to or below the minimum, create Purchase Orders (POs). -> i10:If the PO is created, it needs to be reviewed. -> i9:If the PO is approved, it is printed and released in the system. -> i12:Simultaneously, reserve funds for the released POs and mail the POs to the supplier. -> i14:If the POs are mailed to the supplier, receive the inventory. -> i16:If the inventory is received, proceed to receive the Packing Slip. -> i13:If funds are reserved for the released POs, receive the Packing Slip. -> i15:If the Packing Slip is received, proceed to receive the Invoice. -> i17:If the Invoice is received, proceed to the Three-way match. -> i18:If the Three-way match is successful, release the funds. -> i19:Once the funds are released, issue the payment. -> i20:After the payment is issued, the Resupply Cycle is complete and the process ends.
